1
00:00:01,042 --> 00:00:02,961
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

2
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:05,839
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

3
00:00:09,092 --> 00:00:10,468
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

4
00:00:10,552 --> 00:00:12,721
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

5
00:00:12,804 --> 00:00:16,683
♪ One cut, and it’s over ♪

6
00:00:16,766 --> 00:00:17,559
Yuri: That is Atoy.

7
00:00:17,642 --> 00:00:19,310
Message to Samir.

8
00:00:19,394 --> 00:00:20,937
Tell him not to wait.

9
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:22,480
Atoy: Buddy, Samir's men are there.

10
00:00:22,564 --> 00:00:23,314
Oscar: Huh?

11
00:00:23,398 --> 00:00:24,065
Atoy: Let's hide.

12
00:00:24,149 --> 00:00:24,774
Let's just go over there, buddy.

13
00:00:25,859 --> 00:00:26,860
Ah, I'll stay down here.

14
00:00:26,943 --> 00:00:27,902
Atoy: Okay, okay.

15
00:00:27,986 --> 00:00:28,945
Peping: We have a guest.

16
00:00:29,029 --> 00:00:30,196
[gasping & exclaiming]

17
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:31,448
My goodness! A celebrity, a celebrity?

18
00:00:31,531 --> 00:00:32,407
Who, Father?!

19
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:33,658
The Pope is coming!

20
00:00:33,742 --> 00:00:35,660
[exclaiming & applauding]

21
00:00:35,744 --> 00:00:36,244
[lively chatter]

22
00:00:36,327 --> 00:00:37,954
Samir: Everything that you have moved,

23
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:42,250
the money will allow
us to kidnap the Pope.

24
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:43,585
Dolly: Barangay Tabang Lupa

25
00:00:43,668 --> 00:00:46,004
will be the first casualty.

26
00:00:46,087 --> 00:00:48,381
This is where Master Cutter is from.

27
00:00:48,465 --> 00:00:49,841
So, they will pay for this.

28
00:00:49,924 --> 00:00:50,675
Goon: We need to go.

29
00:00:50,759 --> 00:00:52,093
Atoy is not the reason why we're here.

30
00:00:52,177 --> 00:00:52,844
We go.

31
00:00:52,927 --> 00:00:54,012
[music continues]

32
00:00:54,095 --> 00:00:55,388
Georgia: Is that you?

33
00:00:56,014 --> 00:00:57,182
I'm ready.

34
00:00:58,141 --> 00:01:00,143
Emerson: Bro,
I'm nervous about this mission.

35
00:01:00,226 --> 00:01:01,686
Atoy might mess up.

36
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:04,022
Who is it that you don't
want to catch Atoy?

37
00:01:04,105 --> 00:01:06,149
Samir or Audrey?

38
00:01:06,232 --> 00:01:07,317
Emerson: Of course, his wife.

39
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:09,027
[squealing & panicking]

40
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:10,820
[hushing]

41
00:01:10,904 --> 00:01:11,696
Don't make noise, don't--

42
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:15,700
[squealing & muttering]

43
00:01:16,868 --> 00:01:18,787
Oh-- Audrey?

44
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:21,748
Audrey: I knew it!

45
00:01:22,624 --> 00:01:24,709
Emerson: With Samir,
he can often get past that guy

46
00:01:24,793 --> 00:01:25,960
and he can easily handle him.

47
00:01:26,044 --> 00:01:27,962
- Paldo: True.
- But Mama Mary,

48
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:29,923
she's even sharper than the Obsidians.

49
00:01:30,006 --> 00:01:30,882
Atoy!

50
00:01:30,965 --> 00:01:32,717
I thought you were a good boy?

51
00:01:33,551 --> 00:01:34,427
No!

52
00:01:34,511 --> 00:01:36,763
If-- no-- it’s not what
you're thinking, wrong!

53
00:01:36,846 --> 00:01:38,973
It just so happened
that I got in, and then…

54
00:01:39,057 --> 00:01:40,558
Ah-- anyway!

55
00:01:40,642 --> 00:01:41,768
I'll explain later.

56
00:01:41,851 --> 00:01:42,894
Let's find Audrey first.

57
00:01:42,977 --> 00:01:44,771
- Come on, help me.
- Okay, okay, okay, okay, okay.

58
00:01:44,854 --> 00:01:46,064
Come on. I'll tell Jesabel.

59
00:01:46,147 --> 00:01:47,565
Okay. Where to? Here?

60
00:01:47,649 --> 00:01:49,484
Here, let's go here.

61
00:01:51,402 --> 00:01:54,489
[soft drama music playing]

62
00:01:56,032 --> 00:01:57,951
Atoy: Why does it seem harder now?

63
00:01:58,034 --> 00:02:00,912
[music continues]

64
00:02:01,621 --> 00:02:03,414
I just want to stop Obsidian

65
00:02:03,498 --> 00:02:06,209
and find my fellow trackers.

66
00:02:06,292 --> 00:02:07,418
[music continues]

67
00:02:07,502 --> 00:02:09,504
Barangay officer: What's your name, sir?

68
00:02:10,255 --> 00:02:11,798
What happened?

69
00:02:11,881 --> 00:02:12,841
Atoy: I'm not doing this

70
00:02:12,924 --> 00:02:15,635
just because I want to, or for myself.

71
00:02:15,718 --> 00:02:16,594
[music continues]

72
00:02:16,678 --> 00:02:20,181
But because it is needed
and for the benefit of many.

73
00:02:21,307 --> 00:02:22,892
I just don't want to lose my wife

74
00:02:22,976 --> 00:02:23,893
because of this mission.

75
00:02:23,977 --> 00:02:26,312
[music continues]

76
00:02:26,396 --> 00:02:29,566
You brought us together while I
was in the middle of a mission.

77
00:02:29,649 --> 00:02:30,900
What is that for?

78
00:02:31,401 --> 00:02:33,111
What are you really?!

79
00:02:33,194 --> 00:02:34,988
Now I'll explain to you.

80
00:02:35,071 --> 00:02:37,073
I don't want to listen to you!

81
00:02:37,157 --> 00:02:38,783
Atoy: Everything happened so fast,

82
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:42,579
but meeting her wasn't in my life's plan.

83
00:02:42,662 --> 00:02:44,664
I never forgot you.

84
00:02:44,747 --> 00:02:46,708
So, when we met again?

85
00:02:46,791 --> 00:02:48,418
I came alive again.

86
00:02:49,252 --> 00:02:50,336
Atoy: But sometimes,

87
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:55,258
unplanned things are the best
things that can happen to you.

88
00:02:55,341 --> 00:03:00,013
[sentimental music playing]

89
00:03:00,513 --> 00:03:01,848
Audrey Regalia…

90
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:04,559
will you marry me?

91
00:03:05,268 --> 00:03:07,186
[music continues]

92
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:08,021
Yes.

93
00:03:08,104 --> 00:03:09,355
[exclaiming]

94
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:11,441
Atoy: I wish we could go back to a time

95
00:03:11,524 --> 00:03:13,234
when we had no problems,

96
00:03:13,776 --> 00:03:16,195
when we simply understood each other.

97
00:03:16,738 --> 00:03:20,241
Audrey: I don't know where
we're headed anymore, Atoy.

98
00:03:20,742 --> 00:03:22,577
But I'm only realizing now…

99
00:03:23,995 --> 00:03:26,247
that you're good at pretending.

100
00:03:27,707 --> 00:03:28,583
[music fades]

101
00:03:29,334 --> 00:03:32,420
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

102
00:03:32,503 --> 00:03:36,466
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

103
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:39,219
♪ Wait a moment, Mr. Tailor ♪

104
00:03:39,302 --> 00:03:41,221
♪ Can you be the one to stitch up ♪

105
00:03:41,304 --> 00:03:42,639
♪ The hole in my polo

106
00:03:42,722 --> 00:03:44,807
that's right under the armpit ♪

107
00:03:44,891 --> 00:03:46,851
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

108
00:03:46,935 --> 00:03:48,895
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

109
00:03:48,978 --> 00:03:50,939
♪ If your measurement is wrong,

110
00:03:51,022 --> 00:03:55,276
the whole fit turns crooked… ♪

111
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:56,402
[gunshots]

112
00:03:56,486 --> 00:03:57,862
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

113
00:03:57,946 --> 00:04:00,031
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

114
00:04:00,114 --> 00:04:01,574
[music swells]

115
00:04:03,785 --> 00:04:04,619
[music fades]

116
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:06,996
Emerson: Where's Atoy?

117
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:08,539
- 'Toy!
- Paldo: Well, 'Toy?

118
00:04:08,623 --> 00:04:10,124
'Toy, nothing.

119
00:04:10,792 --> 00:04:11,709
- We didn't see her, 'Toy.
- What?

120
00:04:11,793 --> 00:04:12,627
We didn't see Audrey.

121
00:04:12,710 --> 00:04:13,670
But I've told Jesabel

122
00:04:13,753 --> 00:04:14,963
- in case she sees her.
- She's not there either?

123
00:04:15,588 --> 00:04:16,714
She’s not there, not there.

124
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:18,508
[pensive music playing]

125
00:04:18,591 --> 00:04:21,052
I failed the mission,
and I failed Audrey too.

126
00:04:21,135 --> 00:04:22,178
Son of a--

127
00:04:22,762 --> 00:04:23,721
Ugh!

128
00:04:24,889 --> 00:04:25,974
Atoy, what exactly happened?

129
00:04:26,057 --> 00:04:27,809
How did you end up in Georgia's room?!

130
00:04:28,309 --> 00:04:30,103
Samir's men were chasing me,

131
00:04:30,186 --> 00:04:31,062
and I hid inside.

132
00:04:31,145 --> 00:04:33,189
I didn't know the-- was there--

133
00:04:33,273 --> 00:04:34,524
[music continues]

134
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:37,235
Emerson: You really
have bad luck, don't you?

135
00:04:37,318 --> 00:04:39,028
Ah, Atoy.

136
00:04:40,613 --> 00:04:41,906
Sorry about earlier if…

137
00:04:41,990 --> 00:04:43,616
you and your wife fought.

138
00:04:44,575 --> 00:04:45,827
It was your fault anyway,

139
00:04:45,910 --> 00:04:47,578
why did you enter my room?

140
00:04:47,662 --> 00:04:50,081
Well, I didn't know you were inside.

141
00:04:50,164 --> 00:04:51,582
And you were undressed too.

142
00:04:52,333 --> 00:04:53,626
You were undressed?

143
00:04:53,710 --> 00:04:54,294
Oh, ah--

144
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:55,795
You were undressed?

145
00:04:55,878 --> 00:04:57,046
Oh no!

146
00:04:57,130 --> 00:05:00,174
I get why your wife's angry, 'Toy.

147
00:05:01,217 --> 00:05:02,927
You're in trouble, Atoy.

148
00:05:03,011 --> 00:05:04,679
Why were you undressed anyway?!

149
00:05:05,388 --> 00:05:06,764
It's my room!

150
00:05:07,473 --> 00:05:09,142
And I'm undressed

151
00:05:09,225 --> 00:05:11,644
because I had a massage appointment.

152
00:05:11,728 --> 00:05:14,272
And then, Atoy came in.

153
00:05:14,355 --> 00:05:16,649
I even thought he was the masseur.

154
00:05:18,234 --> 00:05:21,070
Atoy, I'm really sorry.

155
00:05:21,154 --> 00:05:22,655
[soft drama music playing]

156
00:05:22,739 --> 00:05:24,073
Ugh!

157
00:05:24,699 --> 00:05:28,328
[music continues]

158
00:05:28,953 --> 00:05:30,705
Oh, Wanbol, how was your stay here?

159
00:05:30,788 --> 00:05:32,081
Are you happy?

160
00:05:32,165 --> 00:05:32,874
Yes.

161
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:35,168
I hope I can come back again.

162
00:05:35,251 --> 00:05:37,211
Why not? Our house is open to

163
00:05:37,295 --> 00:05:38,588
friends of the family

164
00:05:38,671 --> 00:05:40,590
and family and friends, right?

165
00:05:40,673 --> 00:05:42,341
Janine: Wanbol! Wait, wait!

166
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:43,384
Check Wanbol's bag!

167
00:05:44,385 --> 00:05:45,762
Why, Janine?

168
00:05:45,845 --> 00:05:48,222
Just do it! Check it, Big Sister Karla.

169
00:05:48,306 --> 00:05:50,391
Because he stole something!

170
00:05:50,475 --> 00:05:52,810
Janine, accusing people is bad.

171
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:54,937
You don't want to believe me?

172
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:55,897
Oh, go.

173
00:05:57,857 --> 00:05:59,108
- Stay still!
- Janine--

174
00:05:59,942 --> 00:06:00,818
Where is it?

175
00:06:00,902 --> 00:06:01,819
Do you want proof?

176
00:06:01,903 --> 00:06:02,904
Janine, what are you doing?

177
00:06:02,987 --> 00:06:04,363
Let it be!

178
00:06:04,447 --> 00:06:05,364
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh!

179
00:06:05,448 --> 00:06:07,200
What is this? Oh?

180
00:06:08,451 --> 00:06:10,661
I was right, you really are a thief.

181
00:06:11,454 --> 00:06:13,748
[tense music playing]

182
00:06:14,499 --> 00:06:15,875
Jesabel: Emerson.

183
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:18,377
I've been looking for you for a while now.

184
00:06:18,461 --> 00:06:20,922
Oh, Audrey is
really furious with Sir Atoy.

185
00:06:21,005 --> 00:06:21,881
Emerson: Oh?

186
00:06:21,964 --> 00:06:23,049
Very!

187
00:06:23,633 --> 00:06:24,467
She said that?

188
00:06:24,550 --> 00:06:25,134
Jesabel: Yes!

189
00:06:25,218 --> 00:06:26,469
Atoy's been running around

190
00:06:26,552 --> 00:06:28,554
like crazy looking for her.

191
00:06:28,638 --> 00:06:30,598
She won't even show herself,

192
00:06:30,681 --> 00:06:32,058
and she's in such a bad mood.

193
00:06:32,141 --> 00:06:35,269
Even when I tried to defend Sir Atoy,

194
00:06:35,353 --> 00:06:36,729
nothing, she just got even more annoyed.

195
00:06:36,813 --> 00:06:38,231
All she told me was,

196
00:06:38,314 --> 00:06:40,483
"You know, I'm actually thankful to Oka,

197
00:06:40,566 --> 00:06:43,152
because he immediately told me

198
00:06:43,236 --> 00:06:46,114
where Georgia's room was."

199
00:06:46,197 --> 00:06:48,324
That's exactly how she said it.

200
00:06:48,407 --> 00:06:52,120
Guys, have you seen Atoy?

201
00:06:53,329 --> 00:06:54,330
Audrey and I are together.

202
00:06:54,413 --> 00:06:55,623
She wants to go home already, so

203
00:06:55,706 --> 00:06:56,707
I was just about to take her.

204
00:06:56,791 --> 00:06:57,750
Could you tell him?

205
00:06:58,251 --> 00:07:00,294
Wait. Why are you the one taking her home?

206
00:07:00,378 --> 00:07:02,171
Let her husband take her home!

207
00:07:02,755 --> 00:07:04,006
Where's Audrey?

208
00:07:04,090 --> 00:07:05,424
At the parking lot.

209
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:08,177
Oh, tell her this,

210
00:07:08,261 --> 00:07:10,179
I'll inform Atoy.

211
00:07:10,263 --> 00:07:11,681
Tell her to wait for Atoy and

212
00:07:11,764 --> 00:07:13,391
don't leave without him.

213
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:15,309
Okay, I'll tell her.

214
00:07:15,393 --> 00:07:17,103
[suspicious music playing]

215
00:07:17,186 --> 00:07:17,812
[chuckles]

216
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:21,149
Maybe he should give
me a ride instead, right?

217
00:07:21,232 --> 00:07:22,150
Oh, this woman!

218
00:07:22,233 --> 00:07:22,817
- This woman!
- Jesabel: Oh, come on!

219
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:24,944
- I just missed Oka.
- Look at this, look.

220
00:07:25,027 --> 00:07:25,945
Look, okay?

221
00:07:26,779 --> 00:07:29,198
Oka always tries to
be the hero, doesn't he?

222
00:07:29,282 --> 00:07:31,159
There you go again!

223
00:07:31,242 --> 00:07:32,702
You're being so negative about Oka again.

224
00:07:32,785 --> 00:07:33,786
Exactly.

225
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:35,163
Just because Oka is more handsome.

226
00:07:35,246 --> 00:07:37,248
- He’s more handsome?
- I'm not being negative!

227
00:07:37,331 --> 00:07:38,749
He's the one who's negative.

228
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:40,001
[music continues]

229
00:07:40,084 --> 00:07:41,836
Hmm. Come on, come on, come on.

230
00:07:41,919 --> 00:07:42,503
Where's the equipment?

231
00:07:42,587 --> 00:07:43,754
- Over there, over there.
- Come on, let's go and get it.

232
00:07:43,838 --> 00:07:45,298
- Let's go.
- Come on, Jesabel.

233
00:07:45,381 --> 00:07:46,549
Oka should've been the one with us.

234
00:07:46,632 --> 00:07:48,551
So, Wanbol?

235
00:07:48,634 --> 00:07:50,511
Janine: Why can't you say anything?

236
00:07:50,595 --> 00:07:51,888
Aside from smelling like fish,

237
00:07:51,971 --> 00:07:53,598
you're a thief too!

238
00:07:54,098 --> 00:07:57,685
[soft drama music playing]

239
00:07:57,768 --> 00:08:01,439
Janine, he didn't steal that.

240
00:08:01,522 --> 00:08:03,065
I gave it to him.

241
00:08:04,108 --> 00:08:05,651
I don't believe you.

242
00:08:06,444 --> 00:08:08,404
It's like you're just covering for him.

243
00:08:08,488 --> 00:08:10,114
He's really a thief!

244
00:08:10,823 --> 00:08:13,159
I'm not covering for him.

245
00:08:14,076 --> 00:08:16,120
I gave that to him

246
00:08:16,704 --> 00:08:18,664
so he'd have something

247
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:21,375
for lunch tomorrow at school.

248
00:08:21,459 --> 00:08:22,376
Oh.

249
00:08:23,461 --> 00:08:25,296
Oh, see?

250
00:08:25,379 --> 00:08:27,256
Ibyang was just being kind.

251
00:08:27,798 --> 00:08:29,842
Wanbol didn't steal anything.

252
00:08:30,885 --> 00:08:32,053
Karla: Give it to me.

253
00:08:33,054 --> 00:08:34,305
Apologize, Janine.

254
00:08:35,556 --> 00:08:37,808
You heard her, apologize.

255
00:08:37,892 --> 00:08:40,978
[music swells]

256
00:08:41,062 --> 00:08:41,896
Oh my.

257
00:08:43,564 --> 00:08:47,610
[music continues]

258
00:08:48,528 --> 00:08:51,822
Now she's being dramatic. Aww.

259
00:08:51,906 --> 00:08:52,949
[music fades]

260
00:08:53,032 --> 00:08:55,535
[sneaky music playing]

261
00:08:55,618 --> 00:08:57,578
Sorry about Janine.

262
00:08:57,662 --> 00:08:59,205
Yeah, she's kind of…

263
00:08:59,288 --> 00:09:01,666
you know?

264
00:09:01,749 --> 00:09:02,875
Obnoxious?

265
00:09:02,959 --> 00:09:03,918
Very, yes.

266
00:09:04,001 --> 00:09:05,962
Come on. Gavin is already there.

267
00:09:06,045 --> 00:09:06,796
We'll walk you there.

268
00:09:06,879 --> 00:09:07,463
Let's go.

269
00:09:07,547 --> 00:09:08,130
Come here.

270
00:09:08,214 --> 00:09:09,549
It's Atoy's fault anyway.

271
00:09:09,632 --> 00:09:11,926
Of all the rooms he could've entered,

272
00:09:12,009 --> 00:09:13,302
he had to go into Georgia's room.

273
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:14,428
- Look what happened.
- Oh, no.

274
00:09:15,221 --> 00:09:16,806
Oka was the one who pointed it out

275
00:09:16,889 --> 00:09:19,475
when Samir's men were chasing him.

276
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:21,394
You know, it was
probably just a coincidence.

277
00:09:21,477 --> 00:09:23,271
Because if it weren't for Oka,

278
00:09:23,354 --> 00:09:25,565
Master Cutter would've been caught, right?

279
00:09:26,148 --> 00:09:32,530
[suspicious music playing]

280
00:09:36,492 --> 00:09:38,119
[music fades]

281
00:09:39,328 --> 00:09:43,332
[soft drama music playing]

282
00:09:57,805 --> 00:09:58,639
Tatoy?

283
00:09:59,682 --> 00:10:02,435
[music continues]

284
00:10:05,896 --> 00:10:10,276
[music continues]

285
00:10:36,636 --> 00:10:37,511
Tatoy.

286
00:10:37,595 --> 00:10:38,137
Hmm?

287
00:10:39,221 --> 00:10:40,890
I thought you and Mommy

288
00:10:40,973 --> 00:10:42,600
were spending the night there.

289
00:10:44,143 --> 00:10:45,311
Ah, yeah.

290
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:47,688
Well, because…

291
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:50,816
we missed you.

292
00:10:51,734 --> 00:10:53,527
And I wanted to see you,

293
00:10:53,611 --> 00:10:55,196
I wanted to see Janine.

294
00:10:56,113 --> 00:10:58,908
I want us to be happy.

295
00:10:59,909 --> 00:11:02,953
Like during the picnic, remember?

296
00:11:03,037 --> 00:11:04,997
[music continues]

297
00:11:05,081 --> 00:11:06,040
I missed you.

298
00:11:07,208 --> 00:11:08,876
[music continues]

299
00:11:08,959 --> 00:11:12,088
Hmm, I want that to happen again.

300
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:14,673
But…

301
00:11:15,508 --> 00:11:17,676
Janine is mad at me.

302
00:11:18,844 --> 00:11:22,264
And she's picking on my friend Wanbol too.

303
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:25,267
Oh? You and Janine argued again?

304
00:11:25,893 --> 00:11:27,144
Why?

305
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:29,563
Because…

306
00:11:30,314 --> 00:11:32,191
she thinks

307
00:11:32,274 --> 00:11:34,610
I was the one spreading
a rumor about her at school.

308
00:11:35,903 --> 00:11:38,155
But I didn't do that.

309
00:11:41,617 --> 00:11:44,203
I don't know what else I can do

310
00:11:44,286 --> 00:11:46,330
to make her believe me.

311
00:11:47,373 --> 00:11:48,249
[sighs]

312
00:11:48,332 --> 00:11:49,083
Same.

313
00:11:50,709 --> 00:11:52,711
If only there were some medicine…

314
00:11:53,671 --> 00:11:55,756
that you could buy

315
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:58,551
to make someone believe

316
00:11:58,634 --> 00:12:00,636
that you're not doing anything wrong.

317
00:12:01,929 --> 00:12:03,639
I'd buy it.

318
00:12:06,016 --> 00:12:07,685
But why?

319
00:12:11,689 --> 00:12:14,859
Atoy, they're here.

320
00:12:16,193 --> 00:12:19,447
[somber music playing]

321
00:12:19,530 --> 00:12:21,740
[soft drama music playing]

322
00:12:21,824 --> 00:12:23,909
Ibyang, uhm, go to sleep now, okay?

323
00:12:23,993 --> 00:12:25,661
You and Janine should go to sleep.

324
00:12:25,744 --> 00:12:26,495
Okay?

325
00:12:26,579 --> 00:12:27,913
- Go on, staying up late isn't allowed.
- Yes.

326
00:12:27,997 --> 00:12:29,373
Go on, go to sleep now. [smooches]

327
00:12:29,457 --> 00:12:31,500
[music continues]

328
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:33,669
Good night.

329
00:12:33,752 --> 00:12:35,504
[music continues]

330
00:12:35,588 --> 00:12:36,338
Cita: Come on, Ibyang.

331
00:12:36,422 --> 00:12:37,965
[music continues]

332
00:12:45,973 --> 00:12:46,599
[sighs]

333
00:12:50,811 --> 00:12:51,812
[music fades]

334
00:12:51,896 --> 00:12:53,522
[epic music playing]

335
00:12:53,606 --> 00:12:57,234
I do believe Atoy is innocent.

336
00:12:57,902 --> 00:13:03,157
But if I were in Audrey's situation,

337
00:13:03,657 --> 00:13:06,202
my first reaction would
really be to get angry too.

338
00:13:06,785 --> 00:13:08,454
Just imagine,

339
00:13:08,537 --> 00:13:13,584
my husband and the woman
I suspect is his mistress,

340
00:13:13,667 --> 00:13:15,503
together, half-naked!

341
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:17,505
I'd really declare war against my husband!

342
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:19,507
Why, who is your husband?

343
00:13:20,049 --> 00:13:22,468
Hypothetically speaking, right? If ever!

344
00:13:23,135 --> 00:13:23,886
What's with you, Emerson?

345
00:13:23,969 --> 00:13:25,304
Are you even listening?

346
00:13:25,387 --> 00:13:27,681
You seem really distracted.

347
00:13:27,765 --> 00:13:30,142
[suspicious music playing]

348
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:31,936
Good thing Oka is there.

349
00:13:32,895 --> 00:13:37,149
He can help Atoy calm Audrey down.

350
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:38,192
[music swells]

351
00:13:38,275 --> 00:13:39,985
It's Atoy's fault anyway.

352
00:13:40,069 --> 00:13:42,112
Of all the rooms he could've entered,

353
00:13:42,196 --> 00:13:43,614
he had to go into Georgia's room.

354
00:13:43,697 --> 00:13:45,407
- Look, what happened.
- Oh, no.

355
00:13:45,491 --> 00:13:47,034
Oka was the one who pointed it out

356
00:13:47,117 --> 00:13:49,578
when Samir's men were chasing him.

357
00:13:49,662 --> 00:13:51,205
Have you seen Atoy?

358
00:13:51,288 --> 00:13:52,289
Audrey and I are together.

359
00:13:52,373 --> 00:13:52,873
She wants to go home already,

360
00:13:52,957 --> 00:13:54,583
so I was going to take her.

361
00:13:54,667 --> 00:13:55,417
Could you let him know?

362
00:13:55,501 --> 00:13:56,544
[music fades]

363
00:14:01,215 --> 00:14:02,091
[sighs]

364
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:06,345
Maybe that's exactly
what Oka wanted all along.

365
00:14:06,428 --> 00:14:08,264
What do you mean?

366
00:14:08,347 --> 00:14:10,641
[rousing music playing]

367
00:14:10,724 --> 00:14:13,269
[pensive music playing]

368
00:14:21,777 --> 00:14:23,779
Buddy, I'm sorry.

369
00:14:25,239 --> 00:14:28,534
It's my fault that you and
Audrey ended up fighting.

370
00:14:29,827 --> 00:14:32,079
I didn't know Georgia was there.

371
00:14:32,788 --> 00:14:35,416
[music continues]

372
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:37,376
Atoy: You didn't mean it.

373
00:14:37,459 --> 00:14:39,753
I know you were only trying to save me.

374
00:14:39,837 --> 00:14:43,299
[music continues]

375
00:14:43,841 --> 00:14:46,051
Oscar: Buddy, you and your
wife will work things out.

376
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:47,553
That's normal.

377
00:14:47,636 --> 00:14:49,054
Married couples really do fight.

378
00:14:49,597 --> 00:14:50,097
Right?

379
00:14:50,639 --> 00:14:51,181
[clinks]

380
00:14:52,224 --> 00:14:53,851
Even if we do resolve things…

381
00:14:53,934 --> 00:14:56,228
[sighs]

382
00:14:56,312 --> 00:14:59,231
I still can't tell
her the real reason why I was there.

383
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:03,402
Man, if only I could lay everything
out on the table for her.

384
00:15:04,236 --> 00:15:05,112
[sighs]

385
00:15:05,195 --> 00:15:06,780
Mercado's letter.

386
00:15:06,864 --> 00:15:08,240
[suspicious music playing]

387
00:15:08,324 --> 00:15:10,034
[EXPLOSION & RUMBLES]

388
00:15:10,117 --> 00:15:11,035
[THUDS]

389
00:15:12,953 --> 00:15:14,121
Obsidian.

390
00:15:14,204 --> 00:15:15,372
Ah, no, buddy.

391
00:15:15,873 --> 00:15:18,250
That's exactly what you should never do.

392
00:15:18,334 --> 00:15:19,418
[mysterious music playing]

393
00:15:19,501 --> 00:15:21,378
If Audrey finds out about that…

394
00:15:24,048 --> 00:15:27,426
she won't just stop you
from what you're doing.

395
00:15:28,093 --> 00:15:29,678
Buddy, she'll be scared.

396
00:15:30,721 --> 00:15:33,307
She might even take your
children and leave you.

397
00:15:34,058 --> 00:15:34,850
If that happens, buddy,

398
00:15:34,934 --> 00:15:36,226
you can't blame her.

399
00:15:36,769 --> 00:15:39,813
[music continues]

400
00:15:40,689 --> 00:15:41,357
[sighs]

401
00:15:42,149 --> 00:15:43,692
[music fades]

402
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:45,486
I don't know what to do anymore, buddy.

403
00:15:46,111 --> 00:15:47,446
[suspicious music playing]

404
00:15:47,529 --> 00:15:49,365
I don't want to keep lying to her either.

405
00:15:51,241 --> 00:15:52,368
Buddy, it's like this.

406
00:15:54,536 --> 00:15:56,914
This entire issue is
just about Georgia, right?

407
00:15:58,374 --> 00:15:59,208
That's okay.

408
00:16:01,126 --> 00:16:02,670
Right? Better that than…

409
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:05,214
her finding out
you're fighting terrorists.

410
00:16:06,423 --> 00:16:07,925
Right? You're already in too deep.

411
00:16:08,008 --> 00:16:09,343
[music continues]

412
00:16:09,426 --> 00:16:12,513
I suggest, give Audrey some space.

413
00:16:14,223 --> 00:16:16,308
Oscar: Just finish this mission.

414
00:16:16,392 --> 00:16:18,644
Everything will be back to normal, buddy.

415
00:16:20,938 --> 00:16:22,690
I can help you with that mission too.

416
00:16:22,773 --> 00:16:23,732
Just say the word.

417
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:26,110
[music continues]

418
00:16:26,193 --> 00:16:27,236
Actually, there is something.

419
00:16:28,654 --> 00:16:32,658
Buddy, are you close to your boss at HAI?

420
00:16:33,450 --> 00:16:35,452
Ma'am Dolly?

421
00:16:36,328 --> 00:16:38,038
Hmm. Why, buddy?

422
00:16:38,622 --> 00:16:40,124
[music continues]

423
00:16:40,207 --> 00:16:43,127
She's just a little… suspicious.

424
00:16:43,210 --> 00:16:43,836
Oscar: Hmm?

425
00:16:45,004 --> 00:16:47,089
I suspect she's involved with Obsidian.

426
00:16:47,172 --> 00:16:49,216
[music continues]

427
00:16:50,092 --> 00:16:51,260
Ma'am Dolly?

428
00:16:52,636 --> 00:16:55,848
Buddy, what you're
saying sounds impossible.

429
00:16:56,974 --> 00:16:58,225
Oscar: She’s normal.

430
00:16:58,308 --> 00:17:01,186
She's a normal family
woman, just like Audrey.

431
00:17:03,063 --> 00:17:03,981
But okay, buddy,

432
00:17:05,274 --> 00:17:07,276
if that's what you suspect about her…

433
00:17:08,777 --> 00:17:09,445
all right.

434
00:17:10,112 --> 00:17:11,822
I'll do it for you.

435
00:17:11,905 --> 00:17:12,740
Please, buddy.

436
00:17:12,823 --> 00:17:14,533
[music continues]

437
00:17:14,616 --> 00:17:15,409
[clinks]

438
00:17:15,492 --> 00:17:16,243
I'll keep you updated.

439
00:17:21,957 --> 00:17:23,042
[music fades]

440
00:17:24,334 --> 00:17:25,252
[door lock clicks]

441
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:28,422
[sneaky music playing]

442
00:17:29,131 --> 00:17:29,882
[door closes] Oh.

443
00:17:29,965 --> 00:17:31,675
Uno, check on Master.

444
00:17:31,759 --> 00:17:34,553
I know there's
World War III going on at their house.

445
00:17:36,055 --> 00:17:37,181
Come on.

446
00:17:37,264 --> 00:17:40,434
Let's not interfere in marital disputes.

447
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:42,978
Uno: That's not our business anymore.

448
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:44,021
At the end of the day,

449
00:17:44,104 --> 00:17:47,649
they'll realize they're
family and they love each other.

450
00:17:47,733 --> 00:17:48,484
[music fades]

451
00:17:49,401 --> 00:17:50,652
Uno: They know what to do.

452
00:17:50,736 --> 00:17:53,238
Whoa!

453
00:17:54,281 --> 00:17:57,034
Uno, I didn't know
you had that side to you.

454
00:17:57,117 --> 00:17:59,870
And you're so caring,

455
00:17:59,953 --> 00:18:01,747
you even brought food for me.

456
00:18:01,830 --> 00:18:02,748
Don't be like that.

457
00:18:02,831 --> 00:18:04,041
- That's not for you.
- Jesabel: Soft-hear--

458
00:18:04,666 --> 00:18:05,709
Beatriz!

459
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:07,086
Soft-hear--

460
00:18:07,169 --> 00:18:10,089
The food you requested is here!

461
00:18:10,172 --> 00:18:12,091
It's Beatriz again.

462
00:18:12,174 --> 00:18:13,217
Beatriz!

463
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:15,594
Eat it. Both of you devour it.

464
00:18:15,677 --> 00:18:16,261
[playful music playing]

465
00:18:16,345 --> 00:18:17,346
Beatriz?

466
00:18:17,429 --> 00:18:18,472
Beatriz!

467
00:18:18,555 --> 00:18:20,224
Beatriz, it's always Beatriz.

468
00:18:20,307 --> 00:18:21,266
Uno: Beatriz!

469
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:22,851
Beatriz!

470
00:18:22,935 --> 00:18:24,103
It's always Beatriz, Beatriz.

471
00:18:24,186 --> 00:18:26,313
- It should be Je--
- Jesabel, Beatriz is missing!

472
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:27,314
Come on!

473
00:18:27,397 --> 00:18:28,273
Just leave her alone!

474
00:18:28,357 --> 00:18:30,067
- I'll go look for her.
- She's always wandering around.

475
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:31,819
No, she's just around here somewhere.

476
00:18:31,902 --> 00:18:33,153
Stop looking for her all the time.

477
00:18:33,237 --> 00:18:35,030
You should be looking for me instead.

478
00:18:35,114 --> 00:18:37,116
Jesabel, okay? Jesabel.

479
00:18:37,199 --> 00:18:39,118
Not “Beatriz, Beatriz,
you should eat already!

480
00:18:39,201 --> 00:18:39,701
This is your favorite!”

481
00:18:39,785 --> 00:18:40,869
That's my favorite too.

482
00:18:40,953 --> 00:18:43,413
You should've offered it to me first!

483
00:18:43,497 --> 00:18:44,456
I'm hungry.

484
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:46,125
I'm not going to wait for you two.

485
00:18:46,208 --> 00:18:47,000
[music fades]

486
00:18:47,084 --> 00:18:47,668
Hmm.

487
00:18:48,544 --> 00:18:49,044
[car door closes]

488
00:18:50,754 --> 00:18:51,755
[clears throat]

489
00:19:02,516 --> 00:19:05,769
[rousing music playing]

490
00:19:07,729 --> 00:19:09,148
Oscar: Oh, Emerson? [chuckles]

491
00:19:09,731 --> 00:19:11,400
It's you. I thought…

492
00:19:11,483 --> 00:19:12,818
I thought you'd gone home already.

493
00:19:12,901 --> 00:19:14,194
[chuckles softly]

494
00:19:14,278 --> 00:19:15,988
[crickets chirping in the distance]

495
00:19:19,032 --> 00:19:20,659
Oka, be honest with me.

496
00:19:20,742 --> 00:19:21,410
Oh?

497
00:19:22,035 --> 00:19:24,079
[suspicious music playing]

498
00:19:24,163 --> 00:19:26,790
You really want Audrey and
Atoy to break up, don't you?

499
00:19:26,874 --> 00:19:28,917
[music continues]

500
00:19:29,543 --> 00:19:30,252
Huh?

501
00:19:30,335 --> 00:19:31,795
[chuckles sarcastically]

502
00:19:31,879 --> 00:19:32,838
Hmm.

503
00:19:34,173 --> 00:19:35,299
I've got you all figured out.

504
00:19:36,383 --> 00:19:37,843
A long time ago.

505
00:19:37,926 --> 00:19:39,803
[music continues]

506
00:19:39,887 --> 00:19:42,514
You're the one
who set up Atoy and Georgia.

507
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:45,851
Because you plan to steal Audrey away.

508
00:19:46,351 --> 00:19:46,977
Right?

509
00:19:47,060 --> 00:19:50,230
[music swells]

510
00:19:50,939 --> 00:19:57,112
[tense music playing]

511
00:19:57,196 --> 00:19:57,905
[clicks tongue]

512
00:19:59,323 --> 00:20:00,490
[chuckles]

513
00:20:02,451 --> 00:20:04,745
You know, Emerson,
I can't answer because…

514
00:20:05,329 --> 00:20:06,330
I can't believe

515
00:20:06,413 --> 00:20:08,290
what you're accusing me of.

516
00:20:08,373 --> 00:20:10,292
No, no, no, no, no.

517
00:20:11,585 --> 00:20:13,503
You're the one who led Atoy

518
00:20:13,587 --> 00:20:15,631
to Georgia's cottage,

519
00:20:16,715 --> 00:20:19,343
so Audrey would catch him, right?

520
00:20:20,260 --> 00:20:20,802
Yes.

521
00:20:22,054 --> 00:20:23,305
I pointed him to that cottage,

522
00:20:23,388 --> 00:20:25,307
but not for the reason you're thinking.

523
00:20:26,642 --> 00:20:28,435
But you're also the one who told Audrey

524
00:20:29,728 --> 00:20:31,021
about that cottage.

525
00:20:31,104 --> 00:20:33,523
Because you wanted them
to catch each other, right?

526
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:34,816
[suspicious music playing]

527
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:35,400
[THUDS]

528
00:20:35,484 --> 00:20:37,152
[music continues]

529
00:20:37,236 --> 00:20:38,153
I told Audrey

530
00:20:38,237 --> 00:20:40,030
because she asked me.

531
00:20:40,113 --> 00:20:41,114
But I told her

532
00:20:41,198 --> 00:20:42,574
before I pointed Atoy there,

533
00:20:42,658 --> 00:20:44,618
and how was I supposed
to know Georgia was there?

534
00:20:44,701 --> 00:20:46,453
The door wasn't even locked.

535
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:48,997
Emerson, at that time,

536
00:20:49,081 --> 00:20:51,708
it was urgent because Atoy
needed to hide from Samir.

537
00:20:51,792 --> 00:20:52,960
What’s the matter with you?

538
00:20:53,043 --> 00:20:53,835
[chuckles]

539
00:20:54,586 --> 00:20:55,587
But I'm not a fool,

540
00:20:55,671 --> 00:20:56,922
so don't try to spin me around.

541
00:20:57,422 --> 00:20:58,423
Not me.

542
00:20:58,507 --> 00:21:00,926
[heavy music playing]

543
00:21:16,650 --> 00:21:17,401
You know, Emerson,

544
00:21:17,484 --> 00:21:19,278
ever since I got here…

545
00:21:20,362 --> 00:21:21,947
you've always made me feel

546
00:21:22,030 --> 00:21:23,573
like you don't like me,

547
00:21:24,449 --> 00:21:26,076
like you don't trust me.

548
00:21:28,245 --> 00:21:30,122
Why is that, Emerson?

549
00:21:32,207 --> 00:21:34,042
I've treated you well.

550
00:21:35,252 --> 00:21:36,503
What's the problem?

551
00:21:37,212 --> 00:21:38,880
I don't know either.

552
00:21:38,964 --> 00:21:39,548
[music fades]

553
00:21:39,631 --> 00:21:40,257
Just because.

554
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:41,508
[scoffs]

555
00:21:41,591 --> 00:21:43,593
My gut feeling about you is different.

556
00:21:43,677 --> 00:21:45,429
I can't quite figure it out, but…

557
00:21:45,512 --> 00:21:48,515
your good-boy act doesn't
work on me, bro.

558
00:21:49,933 --> 00:21:51,601
Because you're not genuine.

559
00:21:51,685 --> 00:21:53,812
[suspicious music playing]

560
00:21:53,895 --> 00:21:55,355
That's unfair, bro.

561
00:21:55,439 --> 00:21:57,399
[music continues]

562
00:21:57,482 --> 00:21:58,859
Well, that's my gut feeling.

563
00:21:59,526 --> 00:22:00,777
That's my gut feeling.

564
00:22:02,446 --> 00:22:06,408
So, prove me wrong, okay?

565
00:22:06,992 --> 00:22:08,785
But until you do that…

566
00:22:10,245 --> 00:22:10,829
[clicks tongue]

567
00:22:11,705 --> 00:22:13,373
I'll be watching you, boy.

568
00:22:13,457 --> 00:22:15,167
[cackles]

569
00:22:15,250 --> 00:22:15,959
[clicks tongue]

570
00:22:16,043 --> 00:22:17,878
[cackles]

571
00:22:23,842 --> 00:22:25,135
[music fades]

572
00:22:25,635 --> 00:22:28,096
[rousing music playing]

573
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:30,390
[soft rock music playing]

574
00:22:36,563 --> 00:22:37,606
Hand over your wallet,

575
00:22:37,689 --> 00:22:38,607
and your cellphone too,

576
00:22:38,690 --> 00:22:39,816
if you don't want to get hurt!

577
00:22:39,900 --> 00:22:44,237
Bro, maybe we can talk this through.

578
00:22:44,321 --> 00:22:45,489
[music continues]

579
00:22:45,572 --> 00:22:46,531
Come on!

580
00:22:46,615 --> 00:22:47,783
Are you going to lower it more

581
00:22:47,866 --> 00:22:49,284
or do you want me to do it!?

582
00:22:49,367 --> 00:22:50,786
[thumps & thuds] [grunts & groans]

583
00:22:50,869 --> 00:22:51,995
Well, you're pretty brave!

584
00:22:52,079 --> 00:22:58,001
[grunting &
groaning] [thumping & thudding]

585
00:22:58,085 --> 00:22:58,919
Hey!

586
00:22:59,002 --> 00:22:59,669
[grunts & groans] [thumps]

587
00:22:59,753 --> 00:23:00,295
What?

588
00:23:00,378 --> 00:23:01,171
[grunts]

589
00:23:01,254 --> 00:23:01,838
What?

590
00:23:01,922 --> 00:23:03,882
[grunts & groans]

591
00:23:03,965 --> 00:23:06,426
Huh? Huh?

592
00:23:06,510 --> 00:23:07,344
What?!

593
00:23:07,928 --> 00:23:08,804
What?

594
00:23:08,887 --> 00:23:09,638
Let's go!

595
00:23:09,721 --> 00:23:11,598
- You're ganging up on a woman?
- Let's get out of here!

596
00:23:11,681 --> 00:23:13,934
You idiots!

597
00:23:14,017 --> 00:23:15,268
Come on, come on, hurry!

598
00:23:15,352 --> 00:23:16,311
Leave!

599
00:23:16,394 --> 00:23:19,523
[MOTORCYCLE REVVING]

600
00:23:19,606 --> 00:23:22,109
Didn't I just tell you not to leave?

601
00:23:22,859 --> 00:23:24,194
You're so stubborn.

602
00:23:24,277 --> 00:23:25,904
I got hungry.

603
00:23:25,987 --> 00:23:27,656
I couldn't wait for your food anymore.

604
00:23:28,532 --> 00:23:29,533
Sorry.

605
00:23:30,992 --> 00:23:31,701
[sighs]

606
00:23:32,536 --> 00:23:33,495
Let's go.

607
00:23:34,913 --> 00:23:35,872
Okay.

608
00:23:37,124 --> 00:23:38,291
[rousing music playing]

609
00:23:38,375 --> 00:23:39,584
Belladonna: Where have you been?

610
00:23:40,168 --> 00:23:41,461
[speaks in Russian] Hello.

611
00:23:42,504 --> 00:23:45,507
It's been a long time
since we had a gathering.

612
00:23:46,633 --> 00:23:49,845
Everyone, meet The Washer.

613
00:23:50,345 --> 00:23:52,889
[suspicious music playing]

614
00:23:52,973 --> 00:23:55,100
Samir: She will help
move the money from Zahran

615
00:23:55,183 --> 00:23:56,726
and fund the Big Bang.

616
00:23:57,477 --> 00:24:00,730
Our top priority
now is to find Belladonna.

617
00:24:01,439 --> 00:24:03,567
[music continues]

618
00:24:03,650 --> 00:24:06,194
So, Belladonna is still missing.

619
00:24:06,278 --> 00:24:08,655
[music continues]

620
00:24:09,156 --> 00:24:11,241
But we have

621
00:24:11,324 --> 00:24:13,368
someone on the ground tracking her.

622
00:24:14,202 --> 00:24:15,370
[music continues]

623
00:24:15,453 --> 00:24:18,415
His name is The Soldier.

624
00:24:18,498 --> 00:24:19,749
The Soldier.

625
00:24:20,750 --> 00:24:21,751
Where is he?

626
00:24:22,377 --> 00:24:23,920
I want to meet The Soldier.

627
00:24:24,671 --> 00:24:26,506
You have already met him,

628
00:24:27,340 --> 00:24:29,384
and he knows about you.

629
00:24:30,594 --> 00:24:31,887
What do you mean?

630
00:24:32,429 --> 00:24:34,014
You will find out soon.

631
00:24:37,267 --> 00:24:38,310
[music fades]

632
00:24:38,393 --> 00:24:39,186
He's late.

633
00:24:40,145 --> 00:24:42,397
[tense music playing]

634
00:24:42,480 --> 00:24:44,149
[speaks in Russian] I'm here.

635
00:24:44,983 --> 00:24:46,693
[music swells]

636
00:24:46,776 --> 00:24:47,986
Hello, Ms. Dolly.

637
00:24:49,070 --> 00:24:50,822
Or should I say The Washer?

638
00:24:51,907 --> 00:24:53,283
It's good to see you again.

639
00:24:55,285 --> 00:24:56,536
Oscar?

640
00:24:56,620 --> 00:25:01,166
[music intensifies]

641
00:25:11,051 --> 00:25:13,845
[electronic blipping]

642
00:25:14,554 --> 00:25:18,141
[rousing music playing]

643
00:25:20,268 --> 00:25:21,686
Do you think that's nothing?

644
00:25:21,770 --> 00:25:24,105
Audrey: I saw my husband

645
00:25:24,189 --> 00:25:26,524
with a woman who was naked.

646
00:25:26,608 --> 00:25:28,860
I hope he's really not
cheating on you because…

647
00:25:30,070 --> 00:25:31,404
you don't deserve that.

648
00:25:31,988 --> 00:25:33,406
Ibyang: I'll just find a way

649
00:25:33,490 --> 00:25:37,369
so that you and
Mommy… won't fight anymore.

650
00:25:37,452 --> 00:25:38,328
How?

651
00:25:39,162 --> 00:25:40,789
She won't even talk to me.

652
00:25:41,373 --> 00:25:42,624
Janine: Do you have a plan?

653
00:25:43,416 --> 00:25:44,960
I know what to do.

654
00:25:45,043 --> 00:25:47,212
Dolly: Let me guess your personal mission.

655
00:25:47,295 --> 00:25:48,922
Audrey?

656
00:25:49,005 --> 00:25:51,758
You have to be careful
around the Master Cutter.

657
00:25:51,841 --> 00:25:55,095
If he suspected me, maybe you're next?

658
00:25:55,971 --> 00:25:56,554
What is it, buddy?

659
00:25:56,638 --> 00:25:57,806
What do you need?

660
00:25:58,473 --> 00:26:01,643
Atoy on the phone: Well, we're preparing
a special date for Audrey.

661
00:26:01,726 --> 00:26:05,522
After work, can you head
straight to TL Diner?

662
00:26:05,605 --> 00:26:07,816
[ominous music playing]

663
00:26:07,899 --> 00:26:10,026
Okay, buddy. I'll take care of it.

664
00:26:10,110 --> 00:26:11,653
Atoy on the phone: Thanks, buddy.

665
00:26:12,279 --> 00:26:13,113
[music swells]

666
00:26:13,196 --> 00:26:14,155
Mmm.

667
00:26:14,239 --> 00:26:18,952
[tense music playing]
